        {
          "name": "Paging",
          "description": "Page faults count every call into the fault handler, including zero-fill and copy-on-write faults that need no I/O and faults made to wire memory. Page-ins are file pages read from disk on a fault or by read-ahead; pages a read() call fetches directly are not counted. Page-outs are dirty file pages the pageout daemon wrote back to free memory; write(), fsync and msync writeback are not counted. Anonymous memory is not counted here: it is compressed (Compressions, Decompressions), and the compressor writes it to swap (Swap In, Swap Out, in pages of compressed data). All three charts are pages per second.",
